                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "To determine the rate law when given time and concentration data for a reaction with a single reactant, graph the data and identify which graph yields a linear relationship (straight-line plot).  A zero-order reaction gives a straight-line plot of concentration vs. time with a negative slope. A first-order reaction gives a straight-line plot of ln(concentration) vs. time with a negative slope. A second-order reaction gives a straight-line plot of 1/concentration vs. time with a positive slope.  "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "5kftgmo6hna4dvs",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2960341754"
              },
              "id": "20126274",
              "rule": "input like {.*}",
              "score": 0
            }
